## Historical convergence — before 2026-11-14 correction

The following conclusions apply only to their original observed inputs. Current
states are above; prior bytes remain in the bounded correction preimages.

# Convergence

| Criterion | Requirement / decision / task | State | Observed result | Limit |
| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
| AC-01 | REQ-01 / D-01 / T001 | APPROVED | Ten operational .sh files; two Python files are test code; 32 retired paths have SHA256 preimages and replacements | Bash is the .sh interpreter, with jq/GNU utilities |
| AC-02 | REQ-02 / D-02 / T002 | APPROVED | 89 fast tests, including ten shell acceptance tests and execution of all sixteen controlled adapters; syntax and real ShellCheck pass | Controlled tools prove adapter contracts, not real scanner coverage |
| AC-03 | REQ-03 / D-03 / T003 | APPROVED | Twenty independent-copy, preservation, mutation and export tests pass on disk-backed temporary storage; exact-content authority succession retained | Prior affected approvals remain historical; no product acceptance |
| AC-04 | REQ-04 / D-04 / T004 | INCONCLUSIVE | Five Rust stages, ShellCheck and Gitleaks pass. Seven baseline scanner binaries are unavailable and remain blocked | Full security/quality acceptance requires prepared tools/data/policy; no blanket clean audit |

An early full run exposed generated snapshot links and concurrent input edits during
export; both the transient classification regression and stable-input copy cases
were reexecuted. /tmp quota errors occurred inside and outside the sandbox. The
maintainer authorized disk-backed temporary copies outside the project parent;
all twenty integration cases then passed. Native Rust socket restrictions required
an authorized execution outside the sandbox; six graphical tests remain outside
this non-graphical change and no new GUI acceptance is claimed.

Exact commands, raw logs, input hashes, observed versions and remaining checks are
in docs/validation/scripts-shell-refactor/report.md and evidence.json. No tools
were installed or databases downloaded. No commit or publication.

## Toolchain configuration successor — 2026-11-06

The prior observations are preserved under historical_toolchain_config_evidence.
Affected AC-01..04 are now INCONCLUSIVE on changed script/configuration inputs;
the new implementation and bounded successor evidence belong to
`sdd/features/scripts-toolchain-config/`. No old hashes were renewed.
